<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>gripper_3finger</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version='1.9'>model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
   <name>Aabhash Bhandari</name>
  </author>

  <description>
    Lightweight procedural 3-finger gripper (primitive geometry, no meshes),
    extracted from the original monolithic hillstar/model.sdf so the
    gripper can be composed the same way as rigid_arm_3link.

    This module holds the 3 finger links (collision + visual + contact
    sensor each) plus a palm link that visually/physically connects them -
    but, unlike rigid_arm_3link, it does NOT hold its own joints or the
    GripperController plugin. Two reasons, both about what
    &lt;include merge='true'&gt; can and can't validate/parameterize on its
    own: (1) all 3 finger joints (and the palm joint) parent onto
    "base_link" or an attachment's own tip link, both foreign to this
    module (same constraint that pushed rigid_arm_3link's shoulder joint
    out to its composing file); and (2) GripperController's
    &lt;vehicle_model_name&gt; parameter has to equal whatever the *composed*
    model ends up named (e.g. "hillstar_gripper"), which can't be baked
    into a module meant to be reused as-is. Both the joints and the plugin
    are declared in hillstar_gripper/model.sdf instead - see that file.

    Finger link names are prefixed with this model's own name
    (gripper_3finger/...) so they can't collide with the flattened base
    model's link names once merged - same convention rigid_arm_3link and
    mono_cam/OakD-Lite use.
  </description>
</model>
